WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.180
From tee to green, you've never played golf like this.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:27.940
Welcome to Nostalgia, the only podcast that plays and reviews every NES game released in North America, in chronological order.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.040
I'm Mike.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:30.700
I'm Sean. I'm Joe.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.440
Nice. And Joe is once again joining us via satellite.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.040
And today's episode is all about golf.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.460
So guys, let's talk about some initial impressions.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.780
What do you got, Sean? I was actually pleasantly surprised by golf.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.740
That is just, you know, that's very rewarding to hear because you were the person I was most worried about going into this.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:55.860
Joe and I have talked a little bit on the side about golf and not in depth to the podcast, but like I was worried.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.640
I was like, maybe Sean won't be like as crazy about this game.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:00:59.860
Now, why do you say that?

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.560
That's a, that's a topic for the post show maybe.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:05.440
Um, but let's hear that.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:06.940
Let's hear some more of those initial impressions.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:16.920
Uh, well, I think that, um, this just, I think that this is actually the first game, um, that got golf, right?

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:26.920
Um, cause I did a little, I did a little research on what kind of games came out for like, I don't know, like the Atari and the Intellivision and they look hideous.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:43.300
Okay. And, uh, just, I think the fact that you have so many variables to choose from between like club selection and dealing with the wind and, uh, the actual, um, courses, you know, they're basic, but they do look cool.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:53.720
Um, that this is probably with the technology that they had the best, um, this is the best approximation of golf that I think that they could have done.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.500
Okay. Joe, what do you got?

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:58.720
Uh, yeah, I mean, I kind of, I was also pleasantly surprised.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:03.860
I, at this point we've played two other major sports games, a football game and a baseball game.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:09.260
And I think golf really got it as accurate as it could compared to the other two, especially.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.020
Um, but yeah, it was, it was just a fun game.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:12.960
You know, it was fun golf game.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:14.940
Awesome. All right.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:18.780
So I, I had to, uh, do a little bit of research before I played this.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:29.940
And I just have to mention, uh, that going into this, I had some huge expectations because, uh, golf was designed by Shigeru Miyamoto, uh, of Super Mario Brothers, Legends of Zelda, all that kind of fame.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:39.320
Uh, programmed entirely by, uh, Satoru Iwata, um, president of Nintendo, uh, and also known for so many programming tricks.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:49.420
And, uh, just that, that was incredible on its own, but also all of the sound design in the game is done by Koji Kondo, uh, the Legend of Zelda composer.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:55.000
So you have like three huge names on, on this game already, and I haven't even touched it.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.400
So of course I have big expectations for it.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:08.480
Uh, and when I played, and I'm not a golf guy by any means, but when I played, I, I immediately wanted to know more about how to play this game, how to do it correctly, how to get my score down.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:17.500
Like it, it was intriguing enough because similar to how you were always saying like minimalist football, minimalist baseball, this is minimal golf, but it's minimal golf done right.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:19.400
Like it feels rewarding.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:23.820
So I think like with that, I'll just go really quickly about the objective of the game.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:26.800
For those of you that don't know, uh, it plays exactly.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.800
It plays exactly like real golf.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:37.260
Uh, you play all 18 holes, nine in nine out, and you try to score the lowest score possible by getting your ball in the hole.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.480
Uh, that about covers up the objective.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.440
So let's talk about, uh, the gameplay.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.160
Uh, anybody want to give some gameplay thoughts?

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.300
Yeah. Um, yeah.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.380
Okay. No, this is all you, Joe.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:04:06.140
All right. Um, well, no, I, I just wanted to say that I think the, um, the only thing that initially I thought was a little bit of a hindrance, but really the only problem I had with the gameplay was, um, was turning when you, when you try and turn your angle, it's a pretty, uh, it's a pretty big angle.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.840
Like, like sometimes it's like a compass.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:13.020
Yeah. You know, you only have like, I don't want to go 45 degrees this way or whatever it is.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:20.000
Like I want to kind of go in between, you know, Northwest and I had, uh, I had that problem too, or at least perceived problem.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.220
I think that becomes a lot more of a problem too, though, with the wind.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:26.300
Yeah. Like when wind is not in your favor.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:33.360
Once I took a look at the manual and realized that you can, uh, you can curve the ball, it kind of got a lot easier to kind of correct for that.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:34.400
Like I'd be like, Oh, I'll be here.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:38.960
But since I can't go in between, I'll just kind of go a little to the left and curve it a little to the right.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.240
I did find the curve.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:49.280
The curve is great, but I did find that to sometimes, especially at first, like once I got it down, it was good, but sometimes a little bit of guesswork on which direction.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:53.000
Oh, totally. The ball is going to curve and how much it's going to curve.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:58.080
Yeah. Uh, that's actually, I discovered that because again, I don't usually read the manual.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:02.380
Um, uh, I, I discovered that by just like being bad at it real quick.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:07.000
Like I was curving accidentally and then I realized like, Oh, okay.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:10.660
So this is basically, uh, how you get that fine tuning.

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:18.360
If you, if you really want to like, uh, uh, get around that bunker, um, or make sure you land on that Island correctly.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:25.720
Right. So, um, I think it was, and once I, once I realized that that was a part of the game, like that added so much more depth.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:37.340
Yeah. There's even, uh, going on with that too, with the curve, there's also like a, and I don't know if this is the right word, but like a top spin too, where if you hit early enough, you can, um, you know, you're kind of hitting the ball up higher.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:42.620
So it's, it's actually fighting against the wind a little better to keep that like straight line going.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:48.280
Uh, if so, if you're hitting on the power meter, if you click it, like a lot of,

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:58.620
power and then kind of quick click again, pretty quickly, like before you ever get back to like your center white meter, if you click around there, it'll actually kind of shoot like a pop-up instead.

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:01.020
Because when I like a club thing though.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.740
Yeah. Yeah. It's with the clubs.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:04.060
Yep. Okay. Yeah.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:07.180
Cause there's the, um, I guess the W is for wood.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.760
Is there's the, the PW and S is for iron.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:12.000
Sorry, I'm not a golf double. No, no, it's for wood and iron.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.020
Yep. Right.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.800
So there's a PW and an SW.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:16.560
What are those? Yes. Anyone know?

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.260
I have no idea.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:22.500
And I did not care to research, but I only, I exclusively use those in the bunkers.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:29.820
Yeah. No, I think, uh, I always thought it was like, yeah, power wedge and like, uh, soft wedge, soft wedge.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:31.540
We are not golf.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:32.540
Sounds like a great sandwich.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:36.540
Yeah. Yeah. We're clearly showing that we're not golf people, but that says something that we're not golf people.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:37.620
And we all like this game.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:46.440
Yeah. Um, another little, uh, ingenious piece of, uh, design was how they let you know, um, what kind of slope you're on, on the green.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:53.180
Like at first I thought like, okay, I thought this was just their little texture for showing that you're on the green.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:58.400
Right. Um, but no, like those are arrows that are pointing, um, where the slope is going.

00:06:58.660 --> 00:06:59.520
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.740
There were little, little V's on the green.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:04.320
Yeah. Definitely thought the same that they were like a texture.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.480
Yeah. Right. And it, it wasn't like an,

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:08.740
destructive, like, Oh, here's the arrow on the middle of the screen.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.220
It felt like it was part of the environment that looked like it was.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:16.360
So I was talking about the simplistic nature of the game and I really wanted to kind of break this game down.

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:20.180
So I did break it down into just seven elements and I'd love to share them with you guys.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:24.140
So there's five things you control and there's two things you don't control.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:25.820
And that makes up the entirety of the game.

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:32.620
You control your stance, your club, your swing, your force, and your putt.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:37.560
You don't control the things that are outside are the wind and the obstacles.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:39.800
And that makes up the entirety of the game.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.140
You can describe the whole game in just those seven things.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:51.720
And I think that something about that while relaxing was also like incredibly like, like satisfying to see all work and continue to be like, Oh, I got to try it this way.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.500
This time I got to use this club instead.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:55.540
Like, Oh, the wind is more powerful.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.760
On this course this time.

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:00.000
So I can't get away with using the nine iron, you know?

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:03.060
Yeah. I think that a lot of,

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:09.240
a lot of people now with just the design philosophy of just more content,

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:10.900
more content, more content.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:14.940
people will see the fact that there's only 18,

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:18.240
the old there are only 18 holes and there's not another course.

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:22.520
Like they'll see that as a demerit for the game, but I don't know about you,

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:26.700
but my first playthrough, I had like 60 above par.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:28.640
Oh yeah. No, I was awful,

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:33.580
especially because I just really didn't even understand like which club to use.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:38.400
Like I was using the one wood for the first shot on everything.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:42.880
And then I would just kind of like think like, Oh, this is, I'm pretty close.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:44.980
I should probably, you know, scale down a little bit.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.340
And then I hit like, yeah, I'd overshoot it.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:48.500
I was like, I thought I scaled down.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.880
Yeah, exactly. No, you really have to like scale it.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.780
I'll be honest. I pretty much only use the one wood, the two wedges and the putter.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:57.800
I never used an iron. You never used an iron.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:59.100
I don't know how you did that.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:00.220
That's incredible, Joe.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:04.840
I was, I was almost exclusively using irons after my first one wood.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:08.660
Wow. But I was always shooting for max power too.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.020
Like, like here's why.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:11.300
Okay. Let me explain real fast.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:13.200
Cause I feel like this is definitely worth mentioning.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.260
This game is changed by the manual.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:18.880
And we say that a lot, but when you look at the manual in this game,

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:28.640
it actually has a section that describes how far each club will drive in yards in the bunker and in the green.

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:31.080
So you can kind of assume like, okay.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:37.160
Cause it does tell you that you're like 343 yards away from the, from the hole.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:44.540
Now I wish my one wish for golf on the NES would be that they would have been able to dynamically change that as you got closer.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:47.800
So you would know how many more yards you had to go.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.340
It always says, it always says the same amount.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:55.780
So whatever it was from the start now that makes it kind of like guesswork, but it was also kind of fun too.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:58.440
I was like, okay, well I hit it 180 yards.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:01.200
So I've still got another 200 yards to go.

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:03.060
So I still should use the one wood.

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:09.920
So one thing that, um, I don't think they should have included the, uh, the yardages per, per club.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:16.080
I think that, um, you, that should just be something that you get the feel of throughout the game.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:22.480
Like, oh yeah, I've been using this club and like in my past experience, it allows me to, to go about this far.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:28.680
Or I definitely won't overshoot it if I use this club because it only, it usually only goes about this far.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:33.200
I think that, um, you feel a lot better about your own skill.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:37.520
If you've just, if, if you've like figured this out by yourself, I think.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:40.060
Especially because you could be shooting with different powers.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:43.500
So you might, you know, kind of have a preference with things, you know, you can kind of get your own.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:46.080
Yeah. And I think that's why it's okay that they included it.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.800
Cause there's still a manner of like, you know, and nothing is guaranteed either.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:52.200
Like there's still a matter of preference for your clubs.

00:10:52.400 --> 00:11:01.020
But I think like for me, and this, this might just have been a me thing, but I was kind of having a tough time understanding which club I should use.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.960
Unless I was referring to the manual.

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:07.960
Like it did help to kind of be like, okay, I want to hit this 170 yards.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:12.300
And it was like, not easy for me to just be like, oh yeah, that's the three iron.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:14.780
Like, you know, it's like, I would have, I had to keep going back.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.280
I didn't, I couldn't memorize them.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:18.720
Yeah. I think that's why I sort of, yeah.

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:22.720
I feel like if I played. I think that's why I sort of stuck to the same couple of clubs because.

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:24.980
Okay. Because you knew the power of those clubs.

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:26.740
Yeah. I didn't want to keep looking back at the manual.

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.400
And I was like, okay, I can just adjust how hard I hit this one.

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:30.840
And, you know, these ones do different things.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:38.000
But probably if I were to be playing more often, playing someone like really competitively, I would have to like actually start looking at the other clubs.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:42.120
But, but, you know, I was kind of playing this multiplayer with, with my sister.

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:49.980
And we both started out really bad and both started getting a little better and a little better as we learned the different like intricacies of the controls.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:59.220
Yeah. Going back to like kind of how many things like you input and how many things change and stay the same.

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:10.960
I think even though you've got one course and yeah, there are really only these few things that change from play through to, from play through to play through.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:19.360
I do think that there is a lot of replay value just because I don't know anybody that's going to pick up this game and like just be good at it.

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:20.720
No. Yeah, for sure.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.120
Even if you know golf.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.820
Yeah. I still feel like you're going to be surprised by it.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:29.800
Yeah. Right. Especially the, the, I mean, just, just your swing.

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:36.020
You have, I mean, for a little context too, there's like you, you press A once to start your backswing.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:39.740
You press A again to start coming, you know, to start your forward swing.

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.020
And then you press A.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:47.420
Yeah. I think this game actually codified that as like the actual way to play, make, make golf a game.

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:51.900
Right. And what surprised me though was you press A a third time because there's like a little meter.

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:56.640
And when, when your meter reaches like a little white spot, you want to press A a third time.

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:59.680
That's the ball. So that's like where you want to impact the ball.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:05.580
And what I learned later on was if you, if you hit, if you're early on the impact, it slices,

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:06.600
it curves to the right.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:10.220
Yes. And if you're late, it hooks, it curves to the left.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:13.240
And if you hit it in the, in the white spot, it's a straight shot.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.340
So that like changed the game for us.

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:17.740
Yeah. They're getting a lot out of that one meter.

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:23.160
It kind of, it kind of makes me wish that like, and this is ridiculous, but if like baseball

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:27.860
on the NES had that power meter, you know, where it's like, you kind of are like winding

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:32.500
up for your pitch and then it comes down, you know, it's like so much of like what golf

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:35.260
is implementing here could have been used in almost every other sports game.

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:39.640
Now the, the only thing that kind of bugged me a little bit about, it doesn't really bug

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:40.660
me. I think it works great.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:46.780
I love the control system, but if I think about it logically, the, um, where you hit

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:49.140
the ball has kind of become a timing thing.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:53.820
Like where you hit the ball, it has, has to do with when you press a, which doesn't really

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:54.840
translate to golf.

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:58.400
I mean, I don't know another way around it, but, um, which doesn't, doesn't bother me

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.620
because I don't play golf and it was still fun.

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:02.960
Again, I'm kind of glad that this wasn't like perfect.

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:06.680
Right. When I stepped back to think about that, I was like, wait a minute, that's not how golf

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:09.140
would work, but I think it's not having fun.

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:11.860
I think it simulates as much as it should.

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:18.820
And it leaves all the other stuff, um, on the floor where, where at least if you're trying

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:20.340
to play a video game where it belongs.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.380
How did you guys feel about putting?

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:23.780
I liked putting.

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:30.620
Um, I think that, uh, I had more fun putting than I did, uh, on the rest of the field or

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:32.280
I'm sorry, on the, on the rest of the course.

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:36.960
Um, just because it's a lot more like you're given more information.

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:43.000
Um, you are given more information, but I would argue sometimes that like, you know, as long

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:48.560
as you don't get an out of bounds or a water hazard, making it to the hole, isn't that tough?

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:58.960
It does become tough when you wind up on the green for the putt and you're far from the hole because the power of like what you, you know, like what you have to guess about.

00:14:59.140 --> 00:14:59.940
And I think that's rewarding.

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:07.740
I'm not saying it's bad. I'm saying like the putting for me was harder than the actual, like getting to the hole, like driving through.

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:11.220
I would usually get to the hole in three strokes, three to four strokes.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:15.960
It can definitely get tough when you're far away, especially with like the roll of the

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:20.180
green. Like if you, because if you miss and then, and then you go downhill, you're just going to

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:21.900
go, I mean, sometimes it takes you off the green.

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:23.840
