Gotcha. Uh, okay.

00:29:01.880 --> 00:29:05.000
And I'll go, uh, just to spice it up a little bit.

00:29:05.340 --> 00:29:08.240
Uh, I don't, I shouldn't, I shouldn't always go last.

00:29:08.240 --> 00:29:10.140
I shouldn't always have that, uh, flavor.

00:29:10.360 --> 00:29:11.360
You don't have that power.

00:29:11.560 --> 00:29:14.540
Right. Um, so for me, I don't know.

00:29:14.740 --> 00:29:17.080
I don't know why I became obsessed with this game.

00:29:17.340 --> 00:29:18.560
I don't like golf.

00:29:18.920 --> 00:29:20.880
All right. Golf isn't really for me.

00:29:21.400 --> 00:29:23.480
I, I got a really sore shoulder.

00:29:23.820 --> 00:29:27.880
The one time I like went to like just even drive a driving range.

00:29:27.980 --> 00:29:30.320
Like I've never even played golf, mini golf.

00:29:30.740 --> 00:29:31.660
No one's good at that.

00:29:31.880 --> 00:29:34.080
Like, you know, like that's just the thing that people play.

00:29:34.720 --> 00:29:36.280
Um, well done unless you take it seriously.

00:29:36.480 --> 00:29:37.340
All right. Okay.

00:29:37.880 --> 00:29:38.700
Uh, which is true.

00:29:38.700 --> 00:29:41.280
So I'm sorry to all the mini golf people I insulted.

00:29:41.680 --> 00:29:47.480
Um, this game simplifies so much of golf, but it also retains a surprising bit of depth.

00:29:47.980 --> 00:29:49.880
Uh, there's so many choices you can make.

00:29:49.880 --> 00:29:53.860
And at the same time, they broken it down to only those seven elements that we talked about

00:29:53.860 --> 00:30:02.880
earlier. But, uh, even if the game is rewarding, I just feel like it's still just a 2d NES golf game

00:30:02.880 --> 00:30:08.740
that just because I'm someone who didn't like golf and enjoyed it, I can't guarantee that

00:30:08.740 --> 00:30:13.280
non golf fans all over the world are going to be playing NES golf and be like, this is

00:30:13.280 --> 00:30:15.100
just a fundamentally good game.

00:30:15.100 --> 00:30:21.000
Like we can't say that with certainty just because I do think that what, what has been

00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:25.920
improved on since then, similar to Joe's point, like I've tried some of the PGA tour golf games

00:30:25.920 --> 00:30:30.260
and I do think that they improve on the idea of golf while still keeping it pretty simple.

00:30:30.500 --> 00:30:34.520
You know, nothing is ever as complicated as playing real golf.

00:30:34.600 --> 00:30:35.480
And that's, that's good.

00:30:35.760 --> 00:30:39.680
We would never want a video game to be as realistic as the actual experience.

00:30:39.680 --> 00:30:41.840
It should be a gamified element of it.

00:30:41.840 --> 00:30:46.980
And for that reason, I think that while golf was super fun for me and I had a great time

00:30:46.980 --> 00:30:51.320
with it, I can't recommend this as like a definitive NES game.

00:30:51.560 --> 00:30:58.600
Yeah. I think, um, I actually, um, behind the scenes requested to go last because I could feel myself,

00:30:58.600 --> 00:31:01.880
um, getting really amped up over this game.

00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:04.860
And I knew I was, I was getting drunk off of golf.

00:31:04.860 --> 00:31:13.700
Um, I really didn't want that to, um, make me do a regrettable decision and putting it

00:31:13.700 --> 00:31:14.800
on the essential games list.

00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:21.340
Right. Um, but because I did have a lot of fun, I just like sports games and I'm going to be a

00:31:21.340 --> 00:31:25.980
lot higher on sports games than I think most of us will be.

00:31:25.980 --> 00:31:32.660
Um, just because I, I love the history of, uh, I've talked about this before with baseball

00:31:32.660 --> 00:31:36.860
and tenured fight, like the history of the evolution of trying to simulate the same thing.

00:31:37.460 --> 00:31:46.760
Um, and I think that because of that extended history of sports games outside of any console,

00:31:46.760 --> 00:31:52.060
um, we, there should never, maybe there'll be an exception, but I don't think that there's

00:31:52.060 --> 00:31:56.140
going to be a sports game on our essential games list just because there's always going

00:31:56.140 --> 00:31:56.960
to be a better version.

00:31:57.420 --> 00:32:01.920
Right. Like, uh, PGA tour, uh, with Tiger Woods, like those games.

00:32:02.420 --> 00:32:07.220
I mean, yeah, they're all kind of samey, but they're a lot better than this game.

00:32:07.540 --> 00:32:10.700
Um, and same with every other sport, I think.

00:32:10.900 --> 00:32:15.720
And I think like to that point, we're, we're kind of giving it a resounding play it.

00:32:15.720 --> 00:32:20.260
If you're a fan of NES games, you know, like I, I definitely think it's worth trying if

00:32:20.260 --> 00:32:21.940
you're interested in the NES.

00:32:22.440 --> 00:32:28.060
Uh, but I don't think that like, I can recommend this to someone who's like, just, just like,

00:32:28.120 --> 00:32:29.680
you know, Oh, I like retro games.

00:32:29.680 --> 00:32:31.380
And it's like, you know, uh, yeah.

00:32:31.560 --> 00:32:32.700
I want to play golf.

00:32:32.820 --> 00:32:37.240
Like, you know, it's like, ah, not this, you know, not, not, not this.

00:32:37.640 --> 00:32:42.860
This is the primitive version of everything that's going to come after it, but it just,

00:32:42.940 --> 00:32:45.480
we're just so impressed at how well it does it.

00:32:45.480 --> 00:32:50.840
Right. It seems like we all kind of recommend the game, but can't say it's, it's a must.

00:32:51.040 --> 00:32:52.140
Right. You know? Yeah. Play it.

00:32:52.660 --> 00:32:56.780
It's great. It's fun, but you don't have to, you know, it's not, you're not going to miss out on like

00:32:56.780 --> 00:33:00.120
something, something that's necessary, you know?

00:33:00.220 --> 00:33:01.100
Yep. All right.

